Subject: [PATCH] fix(ip_address): make vrf read-only so updates stop failing on RouterOS 7.21+

Taken from upstream PR #984 against terraform-routeros/terraform-provider-routeros,
applied here to the pinned release v1.99.1 because the fix is not in any release:
upstream's newest tag is v1.99.1 and the PR is open with mergeable_state=blocked.

  issue: https://github.com/terraform-routeros/terraform-provider-routeros/issues/944
  pr:    https://github.com/terraform-routeros/terraform-provider-routeros/pull/984

Why it is needed here, measured on rtr-mikrotik-chateau (RouterOS 7.24.5) on
2026-10-21: RouterOS assigns VRF membership per interface (/ip/vrf holds one
builtin row, `main`, with interfaces=all), so `vrf` on an /ip/address row is a
derived field and its SET endpoint has no such parameter. The provider declares
`vrf` Optional-not-Computed, so refresh stores "main" and every PATCH sends it
back, and RouterOS answers 400 `unknown parameter vrf`. The effect is that **no
attribute of any routeros_ip_address can be updated** - not a comment, not a
network, not `disabled`. Only create and destroy work.

Making the field Computed keeps it readable in state and stops it being sent.

Delete this patch when upstream releases the fix; the build script names the
version to check for.
---
diff --git a/routeros/provider_schema_helpers.go b/routeros/provider_schema_helpers.go
--- a/routeros/provider_schema_helpers.go
+++ b/routeros/provider_schema_helpers.go
@@ -488,6 +488,11 @@
 		Description:      "The VRF table this resource operates on.",
 		DiffSuppressFunc: AlwaysPresentNotUserProvided,
 	}
+	PropVrfRo = &schema.Schema{
+		Type:        schema.TypeString,
+		Computed:    true,
+		Description: "The VRF table this resource operates on.",
+	}
 )

 // PropMtuRw MTU value can be integer or 'auto'.
diff --git a/routeros/resource_ip_address.go b/routeros/resource_ip_address.go
--- a/routeros/resource_ip_address.go
+++ b/routeros/resource_ip_address.go
@@ -54,7 +54,13 @@
 			Computed:    true,
 			Description: "Whether address belongs to an interface which is a slave port to some other master interface",
 		},
-		KeyVrf: PropVrfRw,
+		// vrf is read-only here: RouterOS 7.21+ rejects writes to it on
+		// /ip address rows tied to interfaces that do not carry a VRF
+		// concept (notably WireGuard interfaces, where SET-with-vrf=main
+		// errors with "unknown parameter vrf"). Surfacing it as Computed
+		// keeps the field readable in state without sending it back on
+		// updates. Closes #944.
+		KeyVrf: PropVrfRo,
 	}
 	return &schema.Resource{
 		CreateContext: DefaultCreate(resSchema),
